<title>USA: U.S. sees freeze-damaged wheat, large corn, soy crops.</title>
<headline>U.S. sees freeze-damaged wheat, large corn, soy crops.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agriculture Department, in its first look at this year's crops, forecast a freeze-damaged winter wheat harvest of 1.56 billion bushels Monday and projected a record soybean crop and the second-largest corn crop.</p>
<p>Assuming normal weather and yields, farmers could harvest 2.60 billion bushels of soybeans and 9.84 billion bushels of corn, the department said. Corn and soybean sowings were the largest since the boom times of the early 1980s.</p>
</text>
